console - local terminal escape sequences

DESCRIPTION
    The local display understands a subset of ANSI and VT100 sequences.
    CSI is the escape byte followed by an opening square bracket.

    CSI A B C D       Move the cursor by the given count.
    CSI E F           Move to the start of the next or previous line.
    CSI G d           Set column or row, numbered from one.
    CSI H f           Set row and column, numbered from one.
    CSI J K           Erase the display or line. Mode 0 erases toward
                      the end, 1 toward the start, and 2 the whole area.
    CSI s u           Save or restore the cursor position.
    CSI ?25h ?25l     Show or hide the cursor.
    CSI m             Select text attributes and ANSI colors.

    SGR supports normal and bright ANSI foreground colors, background
    colors, reset, bright text, and reverse video. VGA text fallback
    uses eight background colors. The serial port sends the original
    escape bytes for the attached terminal to interpret.

SEE ALSO
    clear(1), less(1), stty(1), dev(5)
